    "q-152866": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152866",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2}):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14252450/assets/fffe2ba1124b8edd04902db5ad2b0945e5e04372ae0a0ed338c893f0ae417c58.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})$ is $x\\in [2,6].$ This means that $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{2})$ is undefined.",
