    "q-152871": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152871",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\,4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+\\pi )=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of  $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+\\pi :$   \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14252450/assets/42eb38a11d9d63e05c0078bae4c052566b3162571e8563f22cd52ae31bc6dbd7.png)\n\nThe domain of   $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+\\pi $ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=4$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)+\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
